-- coa2-ch2-company-type.l4: Part 5, Chapter 2 (Indications of company type or legal form), ss 58-65,
-- lines 639-742 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.  LAYER 1: the law, objectively; no point of view.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".  Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words.
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the
--               text, limited by its own wording).  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Seams taken as inputs (see PLAN.md section 4): s 4(1), s 4(2), s 3(1) (plain BOOLEAN, the keel answers them without NOTHING),
-- s 88(1) "Welsh company" (this part, ss 88; asked as an input so that this module stands alone), s 1121 "officer in default".
-- Every name that is not in coa-core.l4 begins with the section label it implements.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Required indications for limited companies (ss 58-62)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- s 58(3): community interest companies are outside the section (a flat negative).
-- src:641 | 58 Public limited companies
-- src:642 | (1) The name of a limited company that is a public company must end with “public limited company” or “p.l.c.”.
-- src:643 | (2) In the case of a Welsh company, its name may instead end with “cwmni cyfyngedig cyhoeddus” or “c.c.c.”.
-- src:644 | (3) This section does not apply to community interest companies (but see section 33(3) and (4) of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004 (c. 27)).
@ref s 58(1)-(3) Public limited companies (src:641-644)
GIVEN `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a community interest company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 58(1) the name of the company must end with public limited company or p.l.c.` MEANS
    IF `the company is a community interest company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to community interest companies"
    ELSE IF `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` AND `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The name of a limited company that is a public company"

-- Whether the name ends as the section requires, for a company the section applies to.
-- src:641 | 58 Public limited companies
-- src:642 | (1) The name of a limited company that is a public company must end with “public limited company” or “p.l.c.”.
-- src:643 | (2) In the case of a Welsh company, its name may instead end with “cwmni cyfyngedig cyhoeddus” or “c.c.c.”.
@ref s 58(1)-(2) Public limited companies (the endings) (src:641-643)
GIVEN `the requirement of section 58(1) applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the name ends with “public limited company” or “p.l.c.”` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 88(1) the company is a Welsh company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the name ends with “cwmni cyfyngedig cyhoeddus” or “c.c.c.”` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 58(1) the name of the company ends as the section requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the requirement of section 58(1) applies to the company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF       `the name ends with “public limited company” or “p.l.c.”`
             OR  (`s 88(1) the company is a Welsh company` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the name ends with “cwmni cyfyngedig cyhoeddus” or “c.c.c.”`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE IF `s 88(1) the company is a Welsh company` EQUALS NOTHING AND `the name ends with “cwmni cyfyngedig cyhoeddus” or “c.c.c.”`
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a Welsh company is s 88(1)'s answer and it is not known
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must end with “public limited company” or “p.l.c.”"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section does not apply, so it says nothing about the name
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is not known

-- s 59(3): certain companies are exempt (see section 60); s 59(4): community interest companies are outside the section.
-- src:645 | 59 Private limited companies
-- src:646 | (1) The name of a limited company that is a private company must end with “limited” or “ltd.”.
-- src:647 | (2) In the case of a Welsh company, its name may instead end with “cyfyngedig” or “cyf.”.
-- src:648 | (3) Certain companies are exempt from this requirement (see section 60).
-- src:649 | (4) This section does not apply to community interest companies (but see section 33(1) and (2) of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004).
@ref s 59(1)-(4) Private limited companies (src:645-649)
GIVEN `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a community interest company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 60(1) the private company is exempt from section 59` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59(1) the name of the company must end with limited or ltd.` MEANS
    IF `the company is a community interest company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to community interest companies"
    ELSE IF NOT (`s 3(1) the company is a limited company` AND `s 4(1) the company is a private company`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The name of a limited company that is a private company"
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 60(1) the private company is exempt from section 59`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Certain companies are exempt from this requirement (see section 60)"
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is exempt is s 60(1)'s answer and it is not known

-- src:645 | 59 Private limited companies
-- src:646 | (1) The name of a limited company that is a private company must end with “limited” or “ltd.”.
-- src:647 | (2) In the case of a Welsh company, its name may instead end with “cyfyngedig” or “cyf.”.
@ref s 59(1)-(2) Private limited companies (the endings) (src:645-647)
GIVEN `the requirement of section 59(1) applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the name ends with “limited” or “ltd.”` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 88(1) the company is a Welsh company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the name ends with “cyfyngedig” or “cyf.”` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59(1) the name of the company ends as the section requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the requirement of section 59(1) applies to the company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF       `the name ends with “limited” or “ltd.”`
             OR  (`s 88(1) the company is a Welsh company` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the name ends with “cyfyngedig” or “cyf.”`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE IF `s 88(1) the company is a Welsh company` EQUALS NOTHING AND `the name ends with “cyfyngedig” or “cyf.”`
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a Welsh company is s 88(1)'s answer and it is not known
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must end with “limited” or “ltd.”"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section does not apply, so it says nothing about the name
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is not known

-- s 61 is first because s 60(1)(c) cites it.
-- src:660 | 61 Continuation of existing exemption: companies limited by shares
-- src:661 | (1) This section applies to a private company limited by shares—
-- src:662 | (a) that on 25th February 1982—
-- src:663 | (i) was registered in Great Britain, and
-- src:664 | (ii) had a name that, by virtue of a licence under section 19 of the Companies Act 1948 (c. 38) (or corresponding earlier legislation), did not include the word “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives, or
-- src:665 | (b) that on 30th June 1983—
-- src:666 | (i) was registered in Northern Ireland, and
-- src:667 | (ii) had a name that, by virtue of a licence under section 19 of the Companies Act (Northern Ireland) 1960 (c. 22 (N.I.)) (or corresponding earlier legislation), did not include the word “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives.
@ref s 61(1) Companies to which the section applies (src:660-667)
GIVEN `the company is a private company limited by shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on 25th February 1982 it was registered in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on 25th February 1982 its name, by virtue of a licence under section 19 of the Companies Act 1948 (or corresponding earlier legislation), did not include the word “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on 30th June 1983 it was registered in Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on 30th June 1983 its name, by virtue of a licence under section 19 of the Companies Act (Northern Ireland) 1960 (or corresponding earlier legislation), did not include the word “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(1) the section applies to the company` MEANS
    IF       `the company is a private company limited by shares`
         AND (    (    `on 25th February 1982 it was registered in Great Britain`
                   AND `on 25th February 1982 its name, by virtue of a licence under section 19 of the Companies Act 1948 (or corresponding earlier legislation), did not include the word “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives`)
              OR  (    `on 30th June 1983 it was registered in Northern Ireland`
                   AND `on 30th June 1983 its name, by virtue of a licence under section 19 of the Companies Act (Northern Ireland) 1960 (or corresponding earlier legislation), did not include the word “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to a private company limited by shares" in (a) or (b)

-- The two dates in s 61(1)(a) and (b), as the text states them.
-- src:662 | (a) that on 25th February 1982—
@ref s 61(1)(a) The date for a company registered in Great Britain (src:662-662)
`s 61(1)(a) the date on which the company must have been registered in Great Britain` MEANS Date 25 2 1982

-- src:665 | (b) that on 30th June 1983—
@ref s 61(1)(b) The date for a company registered in Northern Ireland (src:665-665)
`s 61(1)(b) the date on which the company must have been registered in Northern Ireland` MEANS Date 30 6 1983

