    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first condition is that the objects of the company are"

-- src:672 | (4) The second condition is that the company's articles—
-- src:673 | (a) require its income to be applied in promoting its objects,
-- src:674 | (b) prohibit the payment of dividends, or any return of capital, to its members, and
-- src:675 | (c) require all the assets that would otherwise be available to its members generally to be transferred on its winding up either—
-- src:676 | (i) to another body with objects similar to its own, or
-- src:677 | (ii) to another body the objects of which are the promotion of charity and anything incidental or conducive thereto,
-- src:678 | (whether or not the body is a member of the company).
@ref s 61(4) The second condition (src:672-678)
GIVEN `the articles require its income to be applied in promoting its objects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles prohibit the payment of dividends, or any return of capital, to its members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles require all the assets that would otherwise be available to its members generally to be transferred on its winding up to another body with objects similar to its own` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles require all the assets that would otherwise be available to its members generally to be transferred on its winding up to another body the objects of which are the promotion of charity and anything incidental or conducive thereto` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(4) the second condition is met` MEANS
    IF       `the articles require its income to be applied in promoting its objects`
         AND `the articles prohibit the payment of dividends, or any return of capital, to its members`
         AND (    `the articles require all the assets that would otherwise be available to its members generally to be transferred on its winding up to another body with objects similar to its own`
              OR  `the articles require all the assets that would otherwise be available to its members generally to be transferred on its winding up to another body the objects of which are the promotion of charity and anything incidental or conducive thereto`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second condition is that the company's articles— (a) ... (b) ... and (c) ..."

-- src:668 | (2) A company to which this section applies is exempt from section 59 (requirement to have name ending with “limited” or permitted alternative) so long as—
-- src:669 | (a) it continues to meet the following two conditions, and
