-- src:679 | 62 Continuation of existing exemption: companies limited by guarantee
-- src:680 | (1) A private company limited by guarantee that immediately before the commencement of this Part—
-- src:681 | (a) was exempt by virtue of section 30 of the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) or Article 40 of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1032 (N.I. 6)) from the requirement to have a name including the word “limited” or a permitted alternative, and
-- src:682 | (b) had a name that did not include the word “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives,
-- src:683 | is exempt from section 59 (requirement to have name ending with “limited” or permitted alternative) so long as it continues to meet the following two conditions and does not change its name.
@ref s 62(1) Exemption so long as the conditions are met and the name is not changed (src:679-683)
GIVEN `the company is a private company limited by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately before the commencement of Part 5 it was exempt by virtue of section 30 of the Companies Act 1985 or Article 40 of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 from the requirement to have a name including the word “limited” or a permitted alternative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately before the commencement of Part 5 it had a name that did not include the word “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 62(2) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 62(3) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company has changed its name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62(1) the company is exempt from section 59` MEANS
    IF       `the company is a private company limited by guarantee`
         AND `immediately before the commencement of Part 5 it was exempt by virtue of section 30 of the Companies Act 1985 or Article 40 of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 from the requirement to have a name including the word “limited” or a permitted alternative`
         AND `immediately before the commencement of Part 5 it had a name that did not include the word “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives`
    THEN IF       `s 62(2) the first condition is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              AND `s 62(3) the second condition is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              AND NOT (`the company has changed its name`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF       `s 62(2) the first condition is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                  OR   `s 62(3) the second condition is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                  OR   `the company has changed its name`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is exempt from section 59 ... so long as it continues to meet the following two conditions and does not change its name"
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company limited by guarantee that immediately before the commencement of this Part" was exempt and had such a name

-- src:650 | 60 Exemption from requirement as to use of “limited”
-- src:651 | (1) A private company is exempt from section 59 (requirement to have name ending with “limited” or permitted alternative) if—
-- src:652 | (a) it is a charity,
-- src:653 | (b) it is exempted from the requirement of that section by regulations made by the Secretary of State, or
-- src:654 | (c) it meets the conditions specified in—
-- src:655 | section 61 (continuation of existing exemption: companies limited by shares), or
-- src:656 | section 62 (continuation of existing exemption: companies limited by guarantee).
@ref s 60(1) Exemption from requirement as to use of limited (src:650-656)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is exempted from the requirement of section 59 by regulations made by the Secretary of State under section 60` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 61(2) the company is exempt from section 59` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 62(1) the company is exempt from section 59` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(1) the private company is exempt from section 59` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 4(1) the company is a private company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company is exempt"
    ELSE IF       `the company is a charity`
              OR  `the company is exempted from the requirement of section 59 by regulations made by the Secretary of State under section 60`
              OR  `s 61(2) the company is exempt from section 59` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              OR  `s 62(1) the company is exempt from section 59` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF       `s 61(2) the company is exempt from section 59` EQUALS NOTHING
                   OR  `s 62(1) the company is exempt from section 59` EQUALS NOTHING
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether s 61 or s 62 gives the exemption is not known
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A private company is exempt from section 59 ... if— (a) it is a charity, (b) it is exempted ... by regulations ..., or (c) it meets the conditions specified in— section 61 ..., or section 62"

-- src:657 | (2) The registrar may refuse to register a private limited company by a name that does not include the word “limited” (or a permitted alternative) unless a statement has been delivered to him that the company meets the conditions for exemption.
