      `a statement has been delivered to the registrar that the company meets the conditions for exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(2) the registrar may refuse to register the company by the name` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company is a private limited company` AND `the name does not include the word “limited” (or a permitted alternative)`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a private limited company by a name that does not include the word “limited” (or a permitted alternative)"
    ELSE IF `a statement has been delivered to the registrar that the company meets the conditions for exemption`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless a statement has been delivered to him that the company meets the conditions for exemption"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

