-- =========================================================================================================
-- Exempt company: restriction on amendment of articles (s 63)
-- =========================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 63(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 63(1) amend its articles so that it ceases to comply with the conditions for exemption under that section`

-- src:692 | 63 Exempt company: restriction on amendment of articles
-- src:693 | (1) A private company—
-- src:694 | (a) that is exempt under section 61 or 62 from the requirement to use “limited” (or a permitted alternative) as part of its name, and
-- src:695 | (b) whose name does not include “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives,
-- src:696 | must not amend its articles so that it ceases to comply with the conditions for exemption under that section.
@ref s 63(1) Exempt company: restriction on amendment of articles (src:692-696)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is exempt under section 61 or 62 from the requirement to use “limited” (or a permitted alternative) as part of its name` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company's name does not include “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment would make the articles cease to comply with the conditions for exemption under that section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63(1) the company may amend its articles as proposed` MEANS
    IF       `s 4(1) the company is a private company`
         AND `the company is exempt under section 61 or 62 from the requirement to use “limited” (or a permitted alternative) as part of its name` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         AND `the company's name does not include “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives`
         AND `the amendment would make the articles cease to comply with the conditions for exemption under that section`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not amend its articles so that it ceases to comply with the conditions for exemption under that section"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition names only a company within (a) and (b), and only an amendment that ceases to comply

-- The same duty as a prohibition on the company (no time limit; the breach is the offence of s 63(2)).
-- src:692 | 63 Exempt company: restriction on amendment of articles
-- src:693 | (1) A private company—
-- src:694 | (a) that is exempt under section 61 or 62 from the requirement to use “limited” (or a permitted alternative) as part of its name, and
-- src:695 | (b) whose name does not include “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives,
-- src:696 | must not amend its articles so that it ceases to comply with the conditions for exemption under that section.
@ref s 63(1) Exempt company: restriction on amendment of articles (the duty) (src:692-696)
`s 63(1) the company's duty not to amend its articles` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    SHANT `s 63(1) amend its articles so that it ceases to comply with the conditions for exemption under that section`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company amended its articles so that it ceases to comply with the conditions for exemption: an offence is committed under section 63(2)"

-- Who commits the offence: (a) the company and (b) every officer of the company who is in default; a shadow director is
-- treated as an officer for this purpose.  PERSON is a core Party; the officer's default is s 1121's answer (an input).
-- src:697 | (2) If subsection (1) above is contravened an offence is committed by—
-- src:698 | (a) the company, and
-- src:699 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:700 | For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 63(2) Offence (who commits it) (src:697-700)
GIVEN `subsection (1) is contravened` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A Party
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63(2) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`subsection (1) is contravened`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If subsection (1) above is contravened an offence is committed by"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN Company THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `Officer in default` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN Director THEN `liability of an officer`
         WHEN `Company secretary` THEN `liability of an officer`
         WHEN `Shadow director` THEN `liability of an officer` -- "For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company."
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the company and officers in default; it does not say that no one else commits the offence
    WHERE
        `liability of an officer` MEANS
            IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"

-- The text of s 63(3) as rendered runs two wordings of the daily default fine together (line 701): see NOTES.md, fork 1.
-- src:701 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 63(3) Offence (penalty) (src:701-701)
`s 63(3) the penalty on summary conviction` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the rendering shows two wordings and does not choose; see the two functions below
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- The daily default fine on the first wording of s 63(3): "one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale".
-- src:701 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 63(3) Offence (first wording of the daily default fine) (src:701-701)
GIVEN `the amount in pounds of level 5 on the standard scale` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 63(3) the daily default fine in pounds on the first wording` MEANS
    `the amount in pounds of level 5 on the standard scale` DIVIDED BY 10

-- The daily default fine on the second wording of s 63(3): "one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale".
-- src:701 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 63(3) Offence (second wording of the daily default fine) (src:701-701)
GIVEN `the amount in pounds of level 4 on the standard scale` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 63(3) the daily default fine in pounds on the second wording` MEANS
    IF `the amount in pounds of level 4 on the standard scale` GREATER THAN 5000
    THEN `the amount in pounds of level 4 on the standard scale` DIVIDED BY 10
    ELSE 5000 DIVIDED BY 10

-- s 63(4) and s 63(5) are transitional (see NOTES.md): "immediately before the commencement of this section".

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Power to direct change of name in case of company ceasing to be entitled to exemption (s 64)
-- =========================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 64 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 64 change the company's name so that it ends with “limited” or one of the permitted alternatives`

-- src:710 | 64 Power to direct change of name in case of company ceasing to be entitled to exemption
-- src:711 | (1) If it appears to the Secretary of State that a company whose name does not include “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives—
-- src:712 | (a) has ceased to be entitled to exemption under section 60(1)(a) or (b), or
-- src:713 | (b) in the case of a company within section 61 or 62 (which impose conditions as to the objects and articles of the company)—
-- src:714 | (i) has carried on any business other than the promotion of any of the objects mentioned in subsection (3) of section 61 or, as the case may be, subsection (2) of section 62, or
-- src:715 | (ii) has acted inconsistently with the provision required by subsection (4)(a) or (b) of section 61 or, as the case may be, subsection (3)(a) or (b) of section 62,
-- src:716 | the Secretary of State may direct the company to change its name so that it ends with “limited” or one of the permitted alternatives.
@ref s 64(1) Power to direct change of name (src:710-716)
GIVEN `the company's name does not include “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the company has ceased to be entitled to exemption under section 60(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is within section 61 or 62` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the company has carried on any business other than the promotion of any of the objects mentioned in section 61(3) or 62(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the company has acted inconsistently with the provision required by section 61(4)(a) or (b) or 62(3)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(1) the Secretary of State may direct the company to change its name` MEANS
    IF       `the company's name does not include “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives`
         AND (    `it appears to the Secretary of State that the company has ceased to be entitled to exemption under section 60(1)(a) or (b)`
              OR  (    `the company is within section 61 or 62`
                   AND (    `it appears to the Secretary of State that the company has carried on any business other than the promotion of any of the objects mentioned in section 61(3) or 62(2)`
                        OR  `it appears to the Secretary of State that the company has acted inconsistently with the provision required by section 61(4)(a) or (b) or 62(3)(a) or (b)`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If it appears to the Secretary of State that a company whose name does not include “limited” or any of the permitted alternatives— (a) ... or (b) ..., the Secretary of State may direct" (fork 10: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text\'s own no)

-- src:717 | (2) The direction must be in writing and must specify the period within which the company is to change its name.
@ref s 64(2) The direction: in writing, specifying the period (src:717-717)
GIVEN `the direction is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction specifies the period within which the company is to change its name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(2) the direction meets the requirements of subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the direction is in writing` AND `the direction specifies the period within which the company is to change its name`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The direction must be in writing and must specify the period"

-- src:718 | (2A) The period must be a period of at least 28 days beginning with the date of the direction.
@ref s 64(2A) The period: at least 28 days beginning with the date of the direction (src:718-718)
GIVEN `the date of the direction` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(2A) the period meets the requirement of subsection (2A)` MEANS
    IF `the last day of the period` AT LEAST (`the date of the direction` PLUS 27)
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the period beginning with the date of the direction and ending on that day is at least 28 days
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The period must be a period of at least 28 days beginning with the date of the direction"

-- src:719 | (2B) The Secretary of State may by further direction in writing extend the period.
-- src:720 | Any such direction must be given before the end of the period for the time being specified.
@ref s 64(2B) Further direction extending the period (src:719-720)
GIVEN `the further direction is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the further direction` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period for the time being specified` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(2B) the Secretary of State may give a further direction extending the period` MEANS
    IF `the date of the further direction` AT MOST `the last day of the period for the time being specified`
    THEN IF `the further direction is in writing`
         THEN JUST TRUE -- fork 2: a direction given on the last day is given before the end of the period
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by further direction in writing" (fork 18: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text's own no)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any such direction must be given before the end of the period for the time being specified"

-- src:721 | (3) A change of name in order to comply with a direction under this section may be made by resolution of the directors.
-- src:722 | This is without prejudice to any other method of changing the company's name.
@ref s 64(3) Change of name by resolution of the directors (src:721-722)
GIVEN `the change of name is made in order to comply with a direction under section 64` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(3) the company may change its name by resolution of the directors` MEANS
    IF `the change of name is made in order to comply with a direction under section 64`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A change of name in order to comply with a direction under this section"

-- src:722 | This is without prejudice to any other method of changing the company's name.
@ref s 64(3) Without prejudice to any other method (src:722-722)
GIVEN `the company changes its name by another method` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(3) the resolution method does not prejudice another method of changing the name` MEANS
    IF `the company changes its name by another method`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the text says so: "This is without prejudice to any other method of changing the company's name."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence speaks only of other methods

-- src:723 | (4) Where a resolution of the directors is passed in accordance with subsection (3), the company must give notice to the registrar of the change.
-- src:724 | Sections 80 and 81 apply as regards the registration and effect of the change.
@ref s 64(4) Notice to the registrar of a resolution of the directors (src:723-724)
GIVEN `a resolution of the directors has been passed in accordance with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(4) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change` MEANS
    IF `a resolution of the directors has been passed in accordance with subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a resolution of the directors is passed in accordance with subsection (3), the company must give notice to the registrar of the change"

-- The duty to comply with the direction: the period is the one the direction specifies (s 64(2)), here in days.
-- src:725 | (5) If the company fails to comply with a direction under this section an offence is committed by—
-- src:726 | (a) the company, and
-- src:727 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 64(5) Failure to comply with a direction (the duty and its time limit) (src:725-727)
GIVEN `days allowed by the direction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 64 act`
`s 64(5) the company's duty to change its name as directed` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 64 change the company's name so that it ends with “limited” or one of the permitted alternatives`
    WITHIN `days allowed by the direction`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company failed to comply with the direction: an offence is committed under section 64(5)"

-- src:725 | (5) If the company fails to comply with a direction under this section an offence is committed by—
-- src:726 | (a) the company, and
-- src:727 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 64(5) Failure to comply with a direction (who commits the offence) (src:725-727)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with a direction under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A Party
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(5) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company fails to comply with a direction under this section`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company fails to comply with a direction under this section an offence is committed by"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN Company THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `Officer in default` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN Director THEN `liability of an officer`
         WHEN `Company secretary` THEN `liability of an officer`
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names the company and every officer in default; it has no sentence treating a shadow director as an officer here
    WHERE
        `liability of an officer` MEANS
            IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"

